## The train

The rail network is run by ONCF. It links the main towns of the north and centre: Tangier, Rabat, Casablanca, Fez, Meknes, Marrakech and the Oriental region. The train is comfortable, generally punctual and spares you the fatigue of the road.

Since 2018, **Al Boraq**, the high-speed train, has linked Tangier and Casablanca via Kenitra and Rabat, greatly reducing journey times on this route.

{% tip title="Tickets" %}
Buy your tickets at the station or on the official ONCF website. On busy routes (weekends, holidays, festivals), book a few days ahead.
{% /tip %}

## Coaches

The train does not serve the south of the country. To reach Essaouira, Agadir, Ouarzazate, Merzouga or Chefchaouen, coaches are the most practical public transport option. National companies such as **CTM** and **Supratours** run scheduled, air-conditioned services that can be booked in advance. Many private companies complement them, with more variable comfort.

## Taxis

- **Petit taxis** operate within towns. Their colour varies from one town to another. Ask the driver to use the meter, or agree on the fare before setting off.
- **Grand taxis** connect neighbouring towns and villages. They are often shared: you pay for your seat and the taxi leaves when it is full. You can also hire the whole car for more comfort.

## Hiring a car

A car gives you great freedom to explore the Atlas, the valleys and the desert. A few things to keep in mind:

- traffic drives on the right, and police checks are frequent: respect the speed limits;
- mountain roads are winding and sometimes snowy in winter;
- driving at night is not recommended, because of pedestrians, animals and poorly lit vehicles;
- you cannot drive in the medinas: park in a supervised car park.

{% warning title="Before you hire" %}
Check the insurance terms, the excess and the condition of the vehicle when you pick it up. Photograph the car with the rental agent before leaving.
{% /warning %}

## Which option for which route?

- **Tangier, Rabat, Casablanca, Fez, Marrakech**: the train.
- **Marrakech to Essaouira, Agadir or Ouarzazate**: the coach, or a car if you want to stop along the way.
- **A tour of the Atlas and the desert**: a car, or an excursion with a driver.
- **Fez to Chefchaouen**: the coach or a shared taxi.
- **Long distances with little time**: domestic flights between the main airports.

For a complete route idea, see our [two-week itinerary](/en/guides/two-week-morocco-itinerary).
